{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_vl6dd5zgwzpfaz6arpjrv4t3bdhg2r24vihmcuwdbzzudnhgulqq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## Result\n\n**`cargo check`** was already clean — no compile errors in the translation.\n\n### Phase A artifacts (`translation/`)\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | 7 C exports vs 7 Rust exports — **0 missing, 0 extra**, 0 non-libc undefined symbols. No C file untranslated. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **31 rows** mechanically derived from every `return NULL`/`return errno`/`return EXIT_FAILURE`/`perror`/`fprintf(stderr`/unchecked-pointer path. 30 have passing tests; the 1 remaining (`malloc(sizeof(matrix_t))` failing) is unreachable without an allocator fault injector and is marked `n/a`. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 11 branch axes → **36 rows**, all checked. |\n\n### Phases B/C — `tests/phase_b_configs.rs` (36) + `tests/phase_c_errors.rs` (30) = **66 tests, 0 failures**\nBoth `.so`s are `dlopen`ed via `libloading`; Rust is *never* linked directly. Each test compares return value/sentinel, `matrix_t` dims + every cell, the rendered `char*`, written file bytes, **and captured `stderr` bytes** (fd-2 redirection). Randomized rows use xorshift64\\* with a fixed seed. All six low-level entry points are driven directly, not just `driver`.\n\nNotable techniques needed to reach the real C behaviour:\n- **`RLIMIT_AS` capped to 3 GiB** so the `malloc` failures behind `ERRORS.md` rows 2/3/12 happen deterministically instead of overcommit + OOM-kill.\n- **Out-of-process payloads** for the four paths where C legitimately faults (`strdup(NULL)`, `multiply_matrices(NULL,…)`, `free_matrix` on a NULL `matrix` field, `init` after an unchecked failed `allocate_matrix`) — compares exit code, signal *and* stderr.\n- **`/dev/full`** to hit the `fprintf`-fails (ENOSPC, >BUFSIZ) and `fclose`-fails (ENOSPC, <BUFSIZ) branches; `matrix.txt`-as-a-directory to hit `driver`'s write failure.\n- Rendering rows keep values ≤10 chars because the C sizing formula genuinely under-allocates for 11-char values with `width>1`; row 14 exercises `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX` at `width==1`, where the formula fits exactly.\n\n### Phase D\n- `check_symbols.sh` → `SYMBOL PARITY: OK (0 missing)`.\n- `check_features.sh` → no `[features]` table exists, so both the default and `--no-default-features` builds are swept: **ALL FEATURE COMBINATIONS PASSED**.\n- No binary target exists (`add_library` only, no `main`, `crate-type=[\"cdylib\"]`), so the stdout-comparison gate is N/A; `driver()` is instead compared through FFI including the bytes it writes to `matrix.txt`.\n- Suite also passes against `target/debug/libdriver.so`.\n\n### One fix applied\n`translation/Cargo.toml` gained `[profile.dev] debug-assertions = false, overflow-checks = false`. Rust 1.97's debug assertions turned the C-faithful NULL derefs into `SIGABRT` where C gives `SIGSEGV`; release (the shipped artifact) was always correct. No `src/*.rs` change was needed.\n\n### Harness self-validation\n`mutation_check.py` injects 10 deliberate divergences (errno swap, separator off-by-one, 0-based message index, exit-code change, clamped negative width, saturating instead of wrapping arithmetic in two places, added NULL guards, reworded diagnostic) — **10/10 caught**. The two initially-uncaught ones led to new tests (`err_24`/`err_24b`, the `free_matrix` NULL-`matrix`-field rows).\n\n`c_src/` was not modified (only `c_src/build/` output)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1100,"cache_read_input_tokens":197773,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1100,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7dfe309f-5b94-4fba-948d-289ed802c538","uuid":"554f64bf-ccf9-4be2-9421-9a470a0e1d4d","timestamp":"2026-09-05T15:34: